// `std::extensions` (spec/21 §0, D-0187): the implementation-defined
// area. Its submodules, if any, are an implementation's own, documented
// by it; the specification defines nothing here, conformance requires
// nothing of it, and `std`'s root does not re-export it, so a program
// reaches an extension only by naming it (`import std::extensions::x;`),
// where its dependence on this implementation is visible. The reference
// implementation declares nothing here.
